1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,978
Verification needs four inputs: network, public contract address,
verification bundle, and Subscan API key.

2
00:00:06,978 --> 00:00:09,818
This is a real Preview example.

3
00:00:09,818 --> 00:00:13,605
Skip compilation if you already saved the bundle.

4
00:00:14,355 --> 00:00:17,216
Start from the plugin repository checkout.

5
00:00:17,216 --> 00:00:21,985
Install dependencies with npm ci, then run npm run build.

6
00:00:21,985 --> 00:00:24,370
Use Node 22.16 or later.

7
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:27,231
The npm package is currently unpublished.

8
00:00:29,491 --> 00:00:34,310
Use exactly the source deployed on chain, including relative
imports.

9
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:38,165
This two-file example matches our existing Preview deployment.

10
00:00:38,165 --> 00:00:42,021
Source verification makes these selected Compact files public.

11
00:00:43,859 --> 00:00:51,905
Run build with the source directory, entry file, exact compiler
version, and a new output directory.

12
00:00:51,905 --> 00:00:56,934
Version 0.31.1 matches this deployment; choose your own
deployment's version.

13
00:00:56,934 --> 00:01:01,460
The plugin compiles a frozen snapshot and writes verification.json.

14
00:01:03,090 --> 00:01:09,152
Run inspect to check the compiler version, entry file, source
digest, and included files.

15
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:14,347
For a new deployment, preserve the bundle from the same build
artifacts.

16
00:01:14,347 --> 00:01:18,244
For an existing contract, keep its original deployment bundle.

17
00:01:19,689 --> 00:01:23,323
Set SUBSCAN_API_KEY in your shell or CI secrets.

18
00:01:23,323 --> 00:01:26,957
The hidden prompt keeps the key off screen.

19
00:01:26,957 --> 00:01:34,226
A .env file is not loaded automatically; use Node's --env-file
option if you choose that approach.

20
00:01:37,484 --> 00:01:41,478
Set the public hex contract address from your deployment receipt.

21
00:01:41,478 --> 00:01:44,274
Run verify with network, address, and --build-info.

22
00:01:44,274 --> 00:01:51,463
The client reads the API key from the environment and selects the
Subscan API endpoint from the network.

23
00:02:03,564 --> 00:02:08,426
This contract is already-verified, so the real CLI returns already-
verified.

24
00:02:08,426 --> 00:02:10,371
Always check matchesBundle: true.

25
00:02:10,371 --> 00:02:16,693
That confirms the stored source and exact compiler version match
this local snapshot.

26
00:02:17,572 --> 00:02:19,627
Open the returned contract URL.

27
00:02:19,627 --> 00:02:23,737
A pending result means keep checking with the original bundle.

28
00:02:23,737 --> 00:02:26,614
A verification timeout does not require redeployment.

29
00:02:26,614 --> 00:02:30,724
This recording rechecks an existing record without submitting new
source.

30
00:02:31,578 --> 00:02:37,106
On the live Subscan page, confirm Verified Contract and Compact
version 0.31.1.

31
00:02:37,106 --> 00:02:43,554
You have now checked both the matching CLI result and the public
verification status.

32
00:02:43,554 --> 00:02:46,779
Keep your verification bundle for future checks.
